      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To create the `extract_layout.py` script that extracts blocks, lines, tables, or layout elements from a document using a concrete external provider, I will use the Amazon Textract service. Amazon Textract is a machine learning service that automatically extracts text, handwriting, and data from scanned documents. It will be identifiable in the code through the use of the `boto3` library, which is the Amazon Web Services (AWS) SDK for Python, and the specific service client for Textract. </thinking>\n",
